## [{{ version }}]
### Added
- tests: shell unit test for the SBOM handling of yarn-push
- bundles: sbom target merges the app SBOMs from the deploy tree and the core image SBOM into one
  CycloneDX file in deploy/doc, the aarch64 image ships the core image SBOM and the CI template
  .build-bundle-sbom runs the target
- docker/common: the Python library tqem v1.0.0 and squashfs-tools for the sbom target
- go-mod apps: the Go SBOM lists the license of each module, taken from the go-licenses manifest
- docker/README.md: list of the images with their purpose
- app and bundle producers place artifacts into a bin subfolder of the deploy tree, apps keep a flat
  compatibility symlink, preparing the unified deployment layout
- app build archives are placed into the src subfolder of the deploy tree
- new deploy-rc target deploys immutably into the release-candidates tree
- apps/service.mk: all service settings can be set in the app makefile before or after the include;
  settings with an empty value are left out of the service file; new SERVICE_GROUP and SERVICE_RESTART
- apps/service.mk: RUNTIME_RW_PATHS and RUNTIME_RO_PATHS grant the app access to files that other
  units create at runtime, RUNTIME_DEPENDS names these units

### Changed
- ci: base CI templates v4.1.0
- Updated copyright license and file headers
- Breaking changes in package.mk: App services run as an app user instead of root by default,
  set SERVICE_USER=root to keep root
- package and bundle filenames use a stable latest token in snapshot pipelines; local and tag builds
  keep the version-bearing name and the latest symlink
- deps no longer builds the source archive, so the archive is only built where it is published;
  call the archive target to get it
- build jobs take the fetched dependencies from the CI cache; only pipelines that publish the
  source archive build from it
- the source archive of a snapshot pipeline is named <app>_latest.tar.gz, like the package
- common/amd64: patch update for Node and Go
- app SBOMs are deployed below doc/ instead of shipping inside the empkg
- apps/package.mk: service file and manifest generation moved to service.mk and manifest.mk

### Fixed
- apps: a frontend without a software bill of materials no longer breaks yarn-push, the build
  warns and continues
- version.mk: a tag build takes its version from its own tag, even if the commit carries further
  tags
- docker/amd64: update Go and golangci-lint
- docker/common: update nodejs and yarn
